WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.968
Mr. Chancellor,

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.602
this time

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.236
last year,

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.537
I had the privilege of sitting here

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.873
with President Zelensky.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.375
The United States had told him,

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.143
Maybe you shouldn't leave your country

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.578
because something might happen.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.813
But he came in anyway to say

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.515
that our fight is your fight,

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.683
as he did again.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.851
Many nations here,

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.886
with the exception of the US and UK,

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.988
did not believe in the intelligence

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.691
that Vladimir Putin would in fact invade.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.826
And then three days later, it did.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:27.627
You heard

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.628
President Zelensky

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.797
just say, This must be over this year.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.400
Do you share that belief

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.036
that it can and must be?

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:39.139
I think this is really a very brutal war.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.440
It is the imperialistic

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.143
approach of Russia to conquer

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.511
the whole Ukraine

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.713
still or big parts of it.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:50.717
And he is doing this very much furor

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.453
with a lot of brutal

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.789
impact on the soil of the Ukraine.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.525
And many people suffer from that dying

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.127
men, women, children,

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.796
and young and old people.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.697
And this is what we should know.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.166
So this is what we can do

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:07.734
now facing this situation.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.468
And that is

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.670
giving the best support we can.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.239
And this is why Germany enlarged

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.675
constantly its capacity of support

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.843
for the Ukraine.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:19.679
And we did so with the effect that

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.147
now we can say that

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.183
Germany is the biggest supplier

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.385
also of weapons to Ukraine

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.920
in continental Europe.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.089
And we will continue to be there.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.723
But you in your

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:31.257
speech said

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:34.194
we have to be ready for the long haul.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.495
I mean, you must strategize.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.963
You must think among yourselves

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.198
how long this could last.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:40.366
Do you have a target date?

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.634
I think it is wise

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.971
just to be prepared for a long war.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.842
And it is wise to give Putin the message

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:53.079
that we are ready to stay all the time

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.380
together with Ukraine

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.682
and that we will

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.984
constantly support the country.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:02:01.688
So it is not really a very good idea

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.123
that in this conference

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.724
or at this podium,

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.826
the two of us discuss the question

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.628
when exactly in which months

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.396
this war will end.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.666
The really important decision

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:14.434
we should take

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.069
all together is saying

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.238
that we are willing to do it

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.506
as long as necessary

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.341
and that we will do our best.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.108
Do you believe

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:24.677
do you believe

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.913
that NATO's sorry

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.982
the allies will stay united?

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.251
And do you believe that your people

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.619
will stay behind

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:35.388
you and behind this effort?

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.357
Yes.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.258
First,

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:42.061
I am absolutely sure that Putin never

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.864
expected that there would be a

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.566
that the United Europe

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.133
and that there

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.902
would be at that United

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:52.005
what he never thought that

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.107
the transatlantic partnership would work

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.074
that good.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:55.808
But also,

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:56.943
he never thought

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.545
that there would be so much support

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.679
for Ukraine

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.080
from many other countries

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.515
all over the globe.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.350
And he never expected

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.287
that there would be a majority of people

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:08.821
voting in the General Assembly,

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.156
saying that this is a war

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:10.890
against aggression

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.525
that could not be accepted.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.260
And he never expected

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.362
that even in the G20 meeting,

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.264
we had a very strict

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.634
sentence about this war

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.236
and the Russian aggression

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.671
and the absolute

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:25.772
clear sentence

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.773
that nuclear weapons

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.308
should not be used in this war.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.409
So the unity

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:31.711
is someone he never expected.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.112
And it is our task,

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.915
but also our chance that we stick to it.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.951
I am absolutely

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.752
sure that we will.

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.221
And looking at the situation

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.755
in my country,

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.724
I see that there is a broad support

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.226
for the strategy

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:48.328
and activities of the government.

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:49.729
Yes, there are some.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.198
And we are a democratic country

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.733
that are not that sure

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.102
whether it is really a good idea

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.338
to do all these sanctions and to

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.539
and to deploy

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.774
all this many weapons to Ukraine.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:05.878
But even the big majority of those

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.880
is in the end

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.449
accepting that the government

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.184
has to take a responsible

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:12.952
decision and

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.355
trust us in doing what we do.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.358
And even those who possibly sometimes

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:20.827
think we should do something more

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:22.962
really understand

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.564
that it is very good

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:25.732
that we stick together,

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.066
that we never go alone,

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.935
and that we just do it together

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.370
with our friends and partners,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.605
and especially with the United States.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.108
And this is why I'm also sure

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.142
that we will have

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:38.544
the support of our people for the things

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.447
we are having to do.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:43.182
Obviously, one can't put a date

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:43.916
on the end

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.451
However, it does depend,

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.119
I suppose,

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.554
on the amount of help that you send

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.790
and the speed with which you send it.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.658
So no point in

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.226
going over the length of time

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.561
it took to get the leopard tanks

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.030
and for you to say that

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.398
this sort of choreography

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:00.466
between the UK, US and Germany.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.101
But now

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:02.635
you seem to

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.071
be in the position of having to persuade

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.472
all those other countries

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:07.307
that we're trying to get you

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:09.008
to send the leopards or

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:12.078
their leopard to actually send them

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:13.613
why

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.348
to

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:18.718
there is a question

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.853
I have to ask two others,

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.121
especially those

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.324
who were so much urging me

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:26.125
to act in a special way.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:27.827
And I will just repeat,

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.996
the only strategy for being united

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.464
is never doing something

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:32.732
just for your own

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:33.933
and to discuss

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.368
with your friends and partners.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:36.669
And this is what we did.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:39.238
And I really appreciate very much

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.473
the strong alliance

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.475
with the United States in this case.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:43.609
It is very good

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:44.977
that we did a lot

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:47.347
and not just the last step together.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.014
And I'm

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.349
sure we will continue

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.416
to be together

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.919
in this very difficult case.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:53.986
When will they get there?

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.258
When will the tanks get there?

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:01.260
Yours and the others.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.161
So we are working.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.130
The minister of defense is here.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.566
He's working very hard to make it happen.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:08.267
And the industry is doing the same

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.704
so that we are able to deploy the first

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.573
leopard tanks very soon.

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:16.275
And also with trained soldiers.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:18.411
This is what we already started.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.178
And we are doing

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:22.081
so also in giving training and

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:25.985
and support for for all the maintenance

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.754
which is necessary and

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:29.722
ammunition to other parties

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.023
that will join.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.925
And as I learned,

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:35.294
many are not able to deliver the most

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:38.564
modern tanks, which we do.

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:40.433
I hope some more will join

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:42.101
also in this case.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:44.837
But in the ones they are delivering

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:46.873
we will give the support as well.

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:47.640
And as you know,

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:48.474
there is

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.676
also a big number of older tanks

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:52.145
which we will deliver.

00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:54.647
And so this is altogether what we can do

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.517
It's part of our joint activity.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.752
And I am sure that in the end,

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:01.921
it has a

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.689
concrete military

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:07.160
effect But the more most important effect

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:08.661
this case is

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.062
that Putin learns

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:12.231
that it is a miscalculation

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:13.966
if he thinks he can just

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.769
stick to this course as long as necessary

00:07:16.903 --> 00:07:18.871
and then we will stop our support.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.140
This will not happen.

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.042
John Steck, there's

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:26.512
also some worrying information or reality

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:29.715
about your own and generally NATO's

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:31.584
ammunition stockpiles.

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:33.252
Secretary general said

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:34.320
this week said

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.455
what used to take 12

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:36.856
or so months to do

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:38.925
and produce is now taking 28 months.

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:40.860
Is that a worry?

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.129
I mean, they are using a huge amount of

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:44.464
of shells obviously.

00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:45.498
But how

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:46.699
how can you continue

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.801
to prosecute this war

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.503
if you're running out of ammunition

00:07:50.503 --> 00:07:51.404
and the production has

00:07:51.404 --> 00:07:52.772
not yet ramped ramped up

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:57.176
First, I discussed very often visions

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:58.711
and also with Boris,

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.913
the defense minister in Germany,

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:03.483
and my foreign minister, Annalena

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:07.587
that we have to change

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:10.056
the way of dealing with the industry.

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:13.593
So in the last year, more and more

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:16.362
we thought that the relation between

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:20.132
the public Defense Department

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.568
and the industry is something

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:23.436
very similar

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:26.405
to a company that is buying a car.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.208
So there is always a stock of cars

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:31.043
as a permanent production.

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:32.445
There's always what you need

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:33.846
for maintenance

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:35.882
The way we did it in the past,

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:36.516
in the last

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:40.353
20 years or so, is that we once ordered

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:41.621
and we agreed

00:08:41.621 --> 00:08:43.389
that the production is stopping

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:44.357
because

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.659
we have already bought what we need.

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:48.961
So we have to understand

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.596
that for security

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:52.231
we have to change the way

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:53.332
of dealing this fact.

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:55.201
We need a permanent

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:58.137
production of the most important weapons

00:08:58.137 --> 00:08:59.005
we are using.

00:08:59.005 --> 00:09:00.172
And this is also due

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:01.674
to maintenance questions

00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:03.109
and this is also due

00:09:03.109 --> 00:09:05.311
to the question of ammunition.

00:09:05.311 --> 00:09:07.480
And so this is what we are learning.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.548
But learning

00:09:08.548 --> 00:09:10.182
it is means that we are now

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:11.183
taking action

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:13.653
in case of our old defense capabilities,

00:09:13.653 --> 00:09:16.622
but also doing it in supporting Ukraine.

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:18.991
So you already may have heard that

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:19.859
we though

00:09:19.859 --> 00:09:22.695
this is a weapon that has not been used

00:09:22.762 --> 00:09:25.131
and produced for I think, 20 or 30 years.

00:09:26.165 --> 00:09:28.301
We are now producing, again,

00:09:28.935 --> 00:09:30.236
the ammunition for the gap

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:31.237
at Flag Tank,

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:33.372
which is very essential

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:34.640
in defending Ukraine

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.410
from our from from missiles

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.578
and other things.

00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:39.979
And it is something

00:09:39.979 --> 00:09:41.480
which we are starting

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.816
so that there is a constant supply.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.619
We also discuss what we can do

00:09:46.819 --> 00:09:48.220
for achieving the chance

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.021
that the munition

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:50.590
that works with the tanks

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:53.326
that are in use in Ukraine

00:09:53.326 --> 00:09:55.528
most of Eastern and Russian origin

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:57.663
could also be continued.

00:09:57.663 --> 00:09:58.998
And there are a lot

00:09:58.998 --> 00:10:01.534
and I see them of our Eastern partners

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:03.302
who could be very good partners

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:05.738
in creating the production in this case.

00:10:05.972 --> 00:10:08.774
So we are willing to do our best that a

00:10:08.808 --> 00:10:10.676
permanent supply is feasible.

